    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>This simple plugin to display a navigation and panels as a sidebar in WPBakery Page Builder.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin folder to your /wp-content/plugins/ folder.</li>\n<li>Go to the <strong>Plugins</strong> page and activate the plugin.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20use%20this%20plugin%3F'>\nHow do I use this plugin?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>To use the plugin, you just need to activate it. And edit any post/page with the WPBakery Page Builder.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='where%20do%20i%20see%20the%20sidebar%3F'>\nWhere do I see the sidebar?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>The navigation bar will be displayed as a sidebar on the left side of the screen in the WPBakery Page Builder&#8217;s Frontend Editor.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id='how%20do%20i%20disable%20the%20sidebar%3F'>\nHow do I disable the sidebar?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>To disable the sidebar in WPBakery, just deactivate the plugin via the Plugins page in the WordPress dashboard.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Plugin released.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
